<title>SWEDEN: Iceland April air cargo figures rise 18.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Iceland April air cargo figures rise 18.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iceland's international airport at Keflavik handled 1,805 tonnes of freight in April, an 18.5 percent rise over the same month a year earlier, Iceland's civil aviation administration said on Friday.</p>
<p>The administration published the following figures about airport activity for the month.</p>
<p>						    Apr 1997	Apr 1996</p>
<p>KEFLAVIK INT'L AIRPORT</p>
<p> Cargo export (in tonnes)			1,188	   1,029</p>
<p>	 import					  617	     493</p>
<p> Total						 1,805	   1,522</p>
<p> Mail export (in tonnes)			    42		34</p>
<p>	import					   118	     116</p>
<p> Total						   160	     150</p>
<p> Passengers					 67,769	  65,719</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
